# Line endings are normalised in the repository and checked out as LF everywhere.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows commits CRLF and a clone on Linux commits LF, so the same file
# has two identities and every cross-platform diff is whole-file noise. Storing LF and letting Git
# translate on checkout is the portable answer; `text=auto` still leaves Git free to detect binary
# content and leave it alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Except the Windows launcher: cmd.exe parses a .bat by line, and an LF-only batch file misreads
# multi-line constructs. It must keep CRLF on disk.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binaries: never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.jar   binary
*.aar   binary
*.apk   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks   binary

# Generated or vendored, so keep it out of diff summaries and language statistics.
gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar binary linguist-vendored
app/libs/** binary linguist-vendored
